{
    "background_story": "Theodore was a brilliant economist who had spent his entire career studying the intricacies of national budgets. However, his own life was a stark contrast to his professional expertise. Despite his high-paying job, Theodore struggled with a personal deficit - a perpetual shortage of time and energy. His obsessive focus on work had led to a neglect of his physical and mental health, causing him to feel constantly drained. As he approached middle age, Theodore realized that his financial success was not enough to compensate for the deficit in his personal life. He made a conscious effort to rebalance his priorities, taking up meditation and exercise to replenish his depleted reserves. It was a difficult journey, but Theodore eventually found a more sustainable equilibrium, learning that true wealth went beyond mere financial calculations.",
